      "title": "A speech at the Berlin Wall",
      "description": "President Reagan calls for the wall to be opened and removed. The wall remains in place at this point.",
      "source_ids": ["reagan-wall"]
    },
    {
      "month": "1987-10",
      "title": "Black Monday shakes markets",
      "description": "The Dow falls 22.6% in one day. Your chart shows monthly returns, so its October drop is a different number.",
      "source_ids": ["fed-crash1987"]
    }
  ],
  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "Computers were exciting, but the international share basket finished far ahead of Apple and IBM in this window. Disney also rose strongly. The 1987 crash interrupted the journey, although all seven choices still ended above their starting values. This is a reminder that a famous growth story and a high investment return are different things.",
