      "fed-crash1987"
    ]
  },
  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "The recovery and new technology competed for attention with elections, jobs and cultural events. Apple and IBM were easy companies to notice.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "The price paid for an investment mattered alongside its story. A broad basket outside the US beat these famous computer companies over this particular window.",
    "what_faded_away": "Excitement about a movie or a new computer could not settle a five-year investing decision. An interesting headline was only a small piece of information.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "No one knew the date of the coming crash or the final ranking. Diversification spread company risk, but it did not remove market drops.",
